{"id": "c9702_v1_u0_c0_pdf555_1594", "book_title": "Cambridge International AS and A Level Physics Coursebook (2nd edition)", "author": "David Sang, Graham Jones, Gurinder Chadha, Richard Woodside", "unit_no": null, "unit_name": null, "chapter_no": null, "chapter_title": "Appendix 2: Data, formulae and relationships", "section": "Data", "content_type": "appendix", "book_pages": [543, 543], "pdf_pages": [555, 555], "text": "Data\n\nValues are given here to three significant figures, except where more\n\nsignificant figures are useful. speed of light in free space\tc 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹\n\npermeability of free space\tμ₀ 4π × 10⁻⁷ H m⁻¹\n\npermittivity of free space\tε₀ 8.85 × 10⁻¹² C² N⁻¹ m⁻² (F m⁻¹)\n\nelementary charge\te 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C\n\nPlanck constant\th 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s\n\nrest mass of electron\tme 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg\n\nrest mass of proton\tmp 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg\n\nrest mass of neutron\tmₙ 1.675 × 10⁻²⁷ kg\n\nrest mass of α-particle\tmα 6.646 × 10⁻²⁷ kg\n\nmolar gas constant\tR 8.31 J K⁻¹ mol⁻¹\n\nAvogadro constant\tNA 6.02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹\n\nBoltzmann constant\tk 1.38 × 10⁻²³ J K⁻¹ 543 gravitational constant\tG 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ N m² kg⁻²\n\nacceleration of free fall*\tg 9.81 m s⁻²\n\n*Note that this is the value of g which you should use in answering questions;\n\ng varies significantly over the Earth’s surface, with values ranging from 9.78 m s⁻² at the equator to 9.83 m s⁻² at the poles.", "char_count": 929}
{"id": "c9702_v1_u0_c0_pdf555_1595", "book_title": "Cambridge International AS and A Level Physics Coursebook (2nd edition)", "author": "David Sang, Graham Jones, Gurinder Chadha, Richard Woodside", "unit_no": null, "unit_name": null, "chapter_no": null, "chapter_title": "Appendix 2: Data, formulae and relationships", "section": "Conversion factors", "content_type": "appendix", "book_pages": [543, 543], "pdf_pages": [555, 555], "text": "Conversion factors\n\nunified atomic mass unit\t1 u = 1.661 × 10⁻²⁷ kg\n\nelectronvolt\t1 eV = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ J\n\n1 day = 8.64 × 10⁴ s\n\n1 year ≈ 3.16 × 10⁷ s\n\n1 light year ≈ 9.5 × 10¹⁵ m", "char_count": 177}
